# TEST-ONLY FIXTURE. Not loaded by any shipped entrypoint, not part of the deployed deck.
#
# Purpose: the negative control for the G-CACHE pre-boot guard. The real deck Rakefile FORCES
# NO_RAILS_CACHE="true" for every mirror_refresh:* task before config/application is required, and
# ships NO bypass -- so unguarded boot is unreachable through the real Rakefile by design.
#
# Without a way to observe genuinely unguarded boot, the positive examples
# (shared_cache_at_boot=off) would be unfalsifiable: they could be passing because the guard works,
# or because the test environment simply has no live shared cache. This fixture supplies the missing
# half. It loads the SAME application and the SAME mirror_refresh tasks, but deliberately OMITS the
# pre-boot guard block, so a child `rake -f` against it boots with the shared cache live
# (shared_cache_at_boot=on) and reports preboot_guard=absent.
#
# The spec asserts BOTH sides:
#   - real Rakefile + NO_RAILS_CACHE=false  -> shared_cache_at_boot=off, forced-over-caller:false
#   - this fixture  + NO_RAILS_CACHE=false  -> shared_cache_at_boot=on,  preboot_guard=absent
# Layer two (isolate_refresh_cache!) still recovers the run in the fixture case, which is itself
# worth proving.

require File.expand_path("../../../../config/application", __FILE__)

MagiArchive::Application.load_tasks
